    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PageHeader">Runtime</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PageSubheader">Generation, compute engine and prompt compatibility. Configure basic parameters first, then explore advanced settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Section1.Title">Basic generation parameters</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Response">Response</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MaxTokens">Max tokens</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MaxTokens.HelpHint">Maximum response length. Limits how many words the character can write at once. Too long responses fill up the context. Optimal: 300–500 tokens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ReasoningBudget">Reasoning budget</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ReasoningBudget.HelpHint">Hidden reasoning token limit for local models via llama-server. Only works with GGUF models that support reasoning. −1: don't send a limit, keep model default. 0: allocate no tokens for reasoning. Positive number: max reasoning tokens per response; higher values may improve complex answers but slow generation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Temperature">Creativity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Temperature.HelpHint">Temperature (Creativity). Controls the base chaos level in responses. Low (0.1–0.5): logical and predictable. High (0.8–1.5): very creative, emotional and unpredictable. Recommended: 0.8–1.0. At high values, always use Min-P to guard against nonsense.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.TopP.HelpHint">Top-P. Legacy sampling method that limits word selection by cumulative probability percentage. If you use Min-P, always disable Top-P by setting it to 1.0.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Repetition">Repetition</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.FrequencyPenalty">Frequency penalty</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.FrequencyPenalty.HelpHint">Frequency Penalty. Penalizes words based on how many times they already appeared in text. Forces the AI to use rich vocabulary and find synonyms instead of repeating the same adjectives. Too high values break grammar. Optimal: 0.0 - 0.5.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PresencePenalty">Presence penalty</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PresencePenalty.HelpHint">Presence Penalty. Penalizes a word if it appeared at least once. Unlike frequency penalty, this forces the AI to change the conversation topic and introduce new concepts, preventing the dialogue from getting stuck. At high values the AI will chaotically jump between topics. Optimal: 0.0 - 0.4.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Section2.Title">Engine and performance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Engine">Engine</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ServerLaunchCommand">Server launch command</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ServerLaunchCommand.HelpHint">The actual command SoulExe uses to launch the local llama-server. This is a diagnostic field, not a cloud service.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ServerLaunchCommand.ToolTip">Actual llama.cpp launch command</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ComputeBackend">Compute backend</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ComputeBackend.HelpHint">Selects the llama.cpp build: CPU for any PC; CUDA for NVIDIA; Vulkan for compatible GPUs; ROCm for AMD; SYCL for Intel.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Install">Install</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.KVCacheType">KV cache type</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.KVCacheType.HelpHint">Quantize Context Cache to save significant video memory when working with long contexts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MLock">MLock</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MLock.HelpHint">MLock (Memory Lock). This function prevents the language model from being swapped out of RAM to the disk page file. When enabled, the model stays fully loaded in memory, ensuring maximum responsiveness without micro-stutters during generation of each new message. Recommended only when sufficient RAM is available, as this memory will be permanently locked by the system. On low-memory PCs, keep it disabled.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MMAP">Use memory-mapped model (MMAP)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MMAP.HelpHint">Enabled: llama.cpp uses memory-mapped file (mmap) and reads pages from disk on demand. Disabled: No MMAP mode is passed, the model is pre-loaded into RAM; this requires more RAM but may reduce latency during generation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.FlashAttention">Flash Attention</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.FlashAttention.HelpHint">Flash Attention. Latest technology that speeds up generation and reduces VRAM usage when processing long chats. Optimizes neural network computations at large context sizes (4K, 8K and above). Strongly recommended to keep enabled.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ReasoningMode">Reasoning mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ReasoningMode.HelpHint">Reasoning mode (Thinking Mode). Designed for reasoning models like DeepSeek-R1 or QwQ that generate internal reasoning before responding. When enabled, the interface hides &lt;think&gt; tags in a styled block and prevents the TTS engine from reading thoughts aloud. Keep disabled for standard models (Llama-3, Mistral, standard Qwen).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ReasoningMode.Hint">When enabled, configure the reasoning budget above.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Performance">Performance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.GPULayers">GPU layers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.GPULayers.HelpHint">GPU layer offloading. Controls how much of the model is processed by the GPU (VRAM) vs CPU (RAM). More GPU layers means faster generation but higher memory requirements. Especially useful for large models (13B+). If you have a powerful GPU, max it out.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MoELayersOnCPU">MoE layers on CPU</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MoELayersOnCPU.HelpHint">0 = Disabled. Number of Mixture of Experts (MoE) layers placed in system RAM. Critical for MoE architecture models.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ContextSize">Context size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ContextSize.HelpHint">Context window. This is the maximum number of tokens the model can process at once (its working memory). Includes chat history, author notes, and lorebook entries. Larger context allows the character to remember more, but significantly increases VRAM usage. Reduce this value on weak PCs. For long-term memory, keep the Soul Memory module enabled rather than maximizing context.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PromptBatchSize">Prompt batch size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.PromptBatchSize.HelpHint">Number of tokens processed simultaneously during prompt evaluation. 512 is a safe value. Higher values mean faster loading but require more VRAM.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.CPUThreads">CPU threads</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.CPUThreads.HelpHint">0 = Automatic. Specify the number of physical CPU cores for optimal inference speed on processor.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.CustomLlamaCppArgs">Custom llama.cpp arguments</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.CustomLlamaCppArgs.HelpHint">Custom arguments. Allows passing additional command-line arguments directly to the local LLM server (llama.cpp). Intended for advanced users who want to fine-tune specific engine parameters (e.g., RoPE scaling or caching settings) not exposed in the GUI. Use with caution. Invalid flags may crash the server or override interface settings. Example: --rope-freq-base 10000.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Section3.Title">Prompt</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.TemplateAndStopStrings">Template and stop strings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ChatTemplate">Chat template</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.ChatTemplate.HelpHint">Chat Template. Determines the format in which your text is sent to the neural network. Different AIs are trained on different formats. If the template doesn't match the model, the bot will start hallucinating or outputting special characters (e.g., &lt;|im_start|&gt;). Auto takes the template directly from the GGUF file. If the model behaves strangely, manually select ChatML or Llama-3.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.StopStrings">Stop strings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.StopStrings.HelpHint">Stop Strings. A list of words or tags that cause the AI to immediately stop generating when they appear. This is the most important tool to prevent the AI from speaking or acting on your behalf (e.g., generating User: and answering its own questions). Separate with commas. Example: User:, [/s], [eot_id].</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.StopStrings.ToolTip">Separate values with | or a new line</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Section4.Title">Advanced LLM sampling</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.Section4.HelpHint">When this option is disabled, standard generation settings from the first panel are used. Advanced settings are ignored.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MinP">Min-P</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MinP.HelpHint">Min-P (Smart truncation). New gold standard for RolePlay. Dynamically truncates junk words based on the probability of the best word. If the AI is confident, Min-P ruthlessly cuts nonsense. If the AI needs imagination, the barrier lowers to let in beautiful synonyms. Top-P replacement. Set Top-P to 1.0 and Min-P to 0.05 - 0.10 for ideal logic at high Temperature.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MinDynTemp">Min dyn. temp.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.MaxDynTemp">Max dyn. temp.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DynTemp.HelpHint">Dynamic Temperature. Instead of a fixed value, temperature floats between Min. and Max. bounds depending on the AI's confidence. When describing facts, temperature drops for logic. When describing emotions, temperature rises for creativity.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.XTCProbability">XTC probability</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.XTCProbability.HelpHint">XTC (Removing clichés). Revolution for RP. Forcibly removes the most obvious and clichéd words from the AI's options. Tired of phrases like 'goosebumps ran down my spine' or 'predatory grin'? XTC forces the model to find unique, literary alternatives. Probability: chance of algorithm triggering (optimal 0.3 - 0.5).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.XTCThreshold">XTC threshold</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.XTCThreshold.HelpHint">XTC Threshold. Determines how popular (probable) a word must be for the XTC algorithm to be allowed to remove it. Optimal: 0.1 (only words with probability above 10% are removed).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYMultiplier">DRY multiplier</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYMultiplier.HelpHint">DRY (Multiplier). Unlike old algorithms, DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) recognizes and penalizes repetitions of entire sentences and structures. If your waifu keeps starting messages with 'I sigh and look at you', DRY will break this pattern and force her to act differently. Multiplier: penalty strength (optimal 0.8).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYBase">DRY base</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYBase.HelpHint">DRY Base. Base scaling coefficient for the algorithm. Determines how aggressively the penalty grows with the length of the repeated phrase. Optimal: 1.75.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYLengthAllowance">DRY length allowance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DRYLengthAllowance.HelpHint">DRY length allowance. Number of tokens (words/syllables) allowed to repeat before the DRY penalty triggers. Optimal: 2 (to avoid penalizing short connectors like 'I am' or 'And then').</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DynTempExponent">Dyn. temp. exponent</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Settings.DynTempExponent.HelpHint">Dynamic temperature exponent (`dynatemp_exponent`). Separately sets the temperature curve between minimum and maximum values. 1.0 — linear change; above 1.0 holds temperature closer to the lower bound; below 1.0 shifts it faster toward the upper bound.</sys:String>
